  "reasoning": "For Maine\u2019s 2026 U.S. Senate race, the latest University of New Hampshire Pine Tree State Poll (July 15\u201320) shows Democrat Troy Jackson leading incumbent Republican Sen. Susan Collins 49% to 46%, a 3\u2011point Democratic edge within a roughly 3\u2011point margin of error, indicating a statistical tie.[15][16] Earlier polling averages from PollsMax for the prior Democratic nominee Graham Platner showed Collins ahead by 0.5 points (47.3% R to 46.8% D), reinforcing that the race is extremely close and has fluctuated slightly with the candidate change.[11][13] Cook Political Report\u2019s statewide PVI rates Maine as D+4, meaning the state is structurally about four points more Democratic than the national average at the presidential level, but given Collins\u2019s incumbency and the head\u2011to\u2011head polling showing only a narrow Jackson lead, the current evidence supports classifying Maine\u2019s federal lean as a genuine toss\u2011up with a slight Democratic edge in recent polling.[1][10]",
